invariant: INV-26
file: aes.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh aes_traffic
reason: aes_traffic_key_init records AES-128's round count beside the
  AES-256 schedule it expanded, so aes_encrypt_schedule runs a
  TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 key through ten rounds of the wrong cipher.
  Both ends of a chapulin connection would agree with each other and with
  no other implementation, so no loopback notices; the constructor's proof
  asserts the round count each key length writes and the cipher the
  dispatch then runs, and fails on this edit.

--- old
        aes_expand_round_keys_256(key, k->key.round_keys);
        k->key.rounds = AES_256_ROUNDS;
--- new
        aes_expand_round_keys_256(key, k->key.round_keys);
        k->key.rounds = AES_128_ROUNDS;
